1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:03,570
Five days before the outbreak, the warning
arrives between a meme

2
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:05,100
and an argument about pizza.

3
00:00:05,290 --> 00:00:07,740
Buy respirators, spare filters, water.

4
00:00:08,130 --> 00:00:09,330
Don't wait for an announcement.

5
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:10,730
You send a laughing emoji.

6
00:00:10,730 --> 00:00:12,980
Then you ask whether the filters improve your
aim.

7
00:00:13,290 --> 00:00:14,370
Three people react.

8
00:00:14,370 --> 00:00:16,100
The man who sent the warning doesn't.

9
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:17,980
His username is SporeLoser.

10
00:00:18,050 --> 00:00:19,370
His real name is Daniel.

11
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:20,940
You have played together for two years.

12
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:24,540
He works at a research facility and describes
his job as

13
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:26,940
growing things you wouldn't eat.

14
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:30,700
Tonight, he explains, we were studying a
modified fungus.

15
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:32,380
There was a containment failure.

16
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:33,780
People were exposed.

17
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:36,700
Someone posts a mushroom wearing sunglasses.

18
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:38,180
Daniel keeps typing.

19
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:40,100
Confusion, aggression,

20
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:43,570
biting. Avoid contact with anyone showing
symptoms.

21
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:45,420
There may also be an airborne risk.

22
00:00:45,570 --> 00:00:48,020
Someone asks whether this is advertising for a
game.

23
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:51,970
Daniel replies, exposed people may already
have left the facility.

24
00:00:51,970 --> 00:00:54,740
We could see cases across the region within 5
days.

25
00:00:54,850 --> 00:00:57,220
Possibly sooner. You lean back in your chair.

26
00:00:57,850 --> 00:00:58,780
5 days.

27
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:00,700
Very specific for a joke.

28
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,900
You ask why he isn't calling the authorities.

29
00:01:03,090 --> 00:01:04,050
We reported it.

30
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:04,900
That's all I know.

31
00:01:05,050 --> 00:01:07,300
I'm warning you because I don't know what
happens next.

32
00:01:07,530 --> 00:01:09,500
His last message arrives at 9:10.

33
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:10,820
Battery almost gone.

34
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:12,580
Can't safely reach a charging point.

35
00:01:12,930 --> 00:01:13,900
Keeping phone off.

36
00:01:14,090 --> 00:01:15,300
I'll check here tomorrow.

37
00:01:15,370 --> 00:01:16,700
Same time. If I can.

38
00:01:16,810 --> 00:01:17,900
Then he disappears.

39
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:21,540
By midnight, someone has changed the group
picture to a mushroom cloud.

40
00:01:21,650 --> 00:01:22,300
You laugh.

41
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:25,260
At two in the morning, you are still reading
the warning.

42
00:01:25,370 --> 00:01:28,500
You live alone in a detached house at the end
of a quiet street.

43
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:30,540
Good locks. A garage.

44
00:01:30,810 --> 00:01:34,410
A pantry you call your bunker because it
contains six bottles of expensive

45
00:01:34,410 --> 00:01:37,460
wine. Your actual emergency supplies are less
impressive.

46
00:01:37,490 --> 00:01:38,460
Two bottles of water.

47
00:01:39,010 --> 00:01:40,820
A flashlight with dead batteries.

48
00:01:40,930 --> 00:01:42,890
Food that depends on a working freezer.

49
00:01:42,890 --> 00:01:44,090
You close the pantry.

50
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:44,620
Outside,

51
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:47,700
a delivery driver struggles to find your
neighbor's address.

52
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:50,130
Somewhere, a dog is barking.

53
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:52,250
The world looks annoyingly normal.

54
00:01:52,250 --> 00:01:53,100
The following morning,

55
00:01:53,410 --> 00:01:55,620
Daniel has answered none of the new messages.

56
00:01:55,650 --> 00:01:57,100
You search for his facility.

57
00:01:57,250 --> 00:02:00,610
Its website says access is temporarily
restricted because of

58
00:02:00,610 --> 00:02:01,820
an internal incident.

59
00:02:02,090 --> 00:02:04,500
No explanation. You check the publication
time.

60
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:07,300
Last night, you order flashlight batteries.

61
00:02:07,330 --> 00:02:08,980
You aren't preparing for zombies.

62
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:12,610
You're fixing a flashlight At lunch, you add
water to your shopping

63
00:02:12,610 --> 00:02:15,340
list. By evening, the list has a second page.

64
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:16,660
Four days remain.

65
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:19,060
At 9:07, you open the chat.

66
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:20,340
Other people are waiting too.

67
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:21,780
Nobody admits it.

68
00:02:22,130 --> 00:02:22,940
At 9:10,

69
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:24,300
Daniel appears.

70
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:26,060
Did anyone buy supplies?

71
00:02:26,410 --> 00:02:29,340
Someone sends a photograph of mushrooms in a
shopping cart.

72
00:02:29,450 --> 00:02:30,700
Daniel doesn't respond.

73
00:02:31,050 --> 00:02:32,660
A video begins uploading.

74
00:02:32,730 --> 00:02:33,940
23 seconds.

75
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:37,340
the camera points through a narrow window in a
laboratory door.

76
00:02:37,570 --> 00:02:41,180
A man in a torn lab coat stands beside an
overturned trolley.

77
00:02:41,250 --> 00:02:43,420
His identification badge hangs backward.

78
00:02:43,490 --> 00:02:45,690
That's Dr. Harris, Daniel whispers.

79
00:02:45,690 --> 00:02:46,980
I worked with him yesterday.

80
00:02:47,050 --> 00:02:49,540
Someone behind the camera tells Daniel to move
away.

81
00:02:49,730 --> 00:02:50,980
He doesn't. Harris?

82
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,260
The man turns.

83
00:02:52,570 --> 00:02:53,900
Blood covers his chin.

84
00:02:53,970 --> 00:02:55,300
He approaches the glass.

85
00:02:55,530 --> 00:02:57,540
For a second, he looks confused.

86
00:02:57,810 --> 00:02:59,660
Then he throws himself against the door.

87
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:01,380
The camera jerks backward.

88
00:03:01,730 --> 00:03:05,090
Another impact. A woman catches Daniel's
sleeve and pulls him

89
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:05,570
away.

90
00:03:05,730 --> 00:03:07,140
The phone points at the floor.

91
00:03:07,370 --> 00:03:08,420
The video ends.

92
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:10,380
Nobody types for several seconds.

93
00:03:10,730 --> 00:03:11,210
Then,

94
00:03:11,290 --> 00:03:12,940
nice practical effects.

95
00:03:13,250 --> 00:03:14,500
Another message follows.

96
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:15,740
You work in a lab.

97
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:17,660
You literally have costumes.

98
00:03:17,690 --> 00:03:20,300
Someone pauses the video and circles the man's
face.

99
00:03:20,570 --> 00:03:22,420
AI always messes up the skin.

100
00:03:22,530 --> 00:03:23,580
You replay that part.

101
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:26,820
The face is blurred by movement and dirty
glass.

102
00:03:26,930 --> 00:03:29,300
You cannot see what the comment claims to
prove.

103
00:03:29,530 --> 00:03:31,100
You cannot prove the opposite either.

104
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:34,570
Daniel writes, he called his wife yesterday,
asked what they needed

105
00:03:34,570 --> 00:03:35,340
from the store.

106
00:03:35,650 --> 00:03:38,260
Someone replies, tell him to pick up a better
camera.

107
00:03:38,290 --> 00:03:39,900
The laughing reactions begin.

108
00:03:40,130 --> 00:03:43,500
Daniel types, buy the supplies, keep the
receipts,

109
00:03:43,570 --> 00:03:44,930
call me an idiot next week.

110
00:03:44,930 --> 00:03:46,970
You start writing a joke, delete it.

111
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:48,020
What kind of mask?

112
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:51,170
He sends a photograph of packaged respiratory
equipment.

113
00:03:51,170 --> 00:03:52,250
This is what we're using.

114
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:55,610
Correct filters, correct fit, don't assume
anything covering

115
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:56,860
your mouth will protect you.

116
00:03:57,210 --> 00:03:58,650
You ask whether help is coming.

117
00:03:58,650 --> 00:04:00,660
We requested it, we're still waiting.

118
00:04:00,730 --> 00:04:01,210
Then,

119
00:04:01,330 --> 00:04:04,900
tomorrow. Same time, if I can, his status goes
dark.

120
00:04:05,050 --> 00:04:07,860
A film student explains how he would stage the
shot.

121
00:04:08,130 --> 00:04:11,850
Someone posts an AI generated zombie wearing
Daniel's profile

122
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:15,610
picture. Within 10 minutes, they are arguing
about something unrelated.

123
00:04:15,610 --> 00:04:17,980
You return to the video, not the blood,

124
00:04:18,330 --> 00:04:19,940
the woman pulling Daniel away,

125
00:04:20,370 --> 00:04:21,500
Her hand shakes.

126
00:04:21,690 --> 00:04:23,420
She misses his sleeve the first time.

127
00:04:23,570 --> 00:04:24,940
You watch that moment again.

128
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:26,300
It could still be acting.

129
00:04:26,490 --> 00:04:28,300
You wish that thought made you feel better.

130
00:04:28,450 --> 00:04:29,860
You open your shopping list.

131
00:04:30,010 --> 00:04:32,330
Delete the question mark beside respirator.

132
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:32,980
The next morning,

133
00:04:33,290 --> 00:04:34,300
three days remain.

134
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:36,380
You visit a safety equipment supplier.

135
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:38,090
You show him Daniel's photograph.

136
00:04:38,090 --> 00:04:41,380
He checks the model and explains the filters,
sizing,

137
00:04:41,450 --> 00:04:43,780
and limitations. You ask about fitting.

138
00:04:43,850 --> 00:04:45,740
He makes you take off the sunglasses.

139
00:04:45,970 --> 00:04:46,450
For once,

140
00:04:46,850 --> 00:04:49,810
somebody has advice you can use without
believing in monsters.

141
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:50,340
Outside,

142
00:04:50,650 --> 00:04:51,940
your phone vibrates.

143
00:04:52,290 --> 00:04:54,460
Another video. This one isn't from Daniel.

144
00:04:54,490 --> 00:04:57,050
40 seconds, filmed through a bus window.

145
00:04:57,050 --> 00:05:00,020
A man in hospital trousers runs across an
intersection.

146
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:01,620
Two people try to restrain him.

147
00:05:01,770 --> 00:05:03,060
He bites one of them in the face.

148
00:05:03,330 --> 00:05:04,620
The camera jerks away.

149
00:05:04,970 --> 00:05:05,900
When it turns back,

150
00:05:06,290 --> 00:05:07,780
somebody else is on the pavement.

151
00:05:07,930 --> 00:05:10,020
The intersection is identified in the
comments.

152
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:12,050
Less than an hour from the facility.

153
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:13,140
you open the link again,

154
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:15,180
unavailable. Back in the group,

155
00:05:15,450 --> 00:05:16,730
four people have saved it.

156
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:18,460
Copies appear on other accounts.

157
00:05:18,690 --> 00:05:20,540
Half the comments say drugs.

158
00:05:20,650 --> 00:05:22,060
The other half say AI.

159
00:05:22,250 --> 00:05:24,620
Someone circles a hand with six fingers.

160
00:05:24,770 --> 00:05:26,460
A clearer upload shows five.

161
00:05:26,770 --> 00:05:28,290
You hate yourself for counting.

162
00:05:28,290 --> 00:05:30,260
One video disappearing proves little.

163
00:05:30,410 --> 00:05:33,810
But the warning, the closed facility, and
footage from a

164
00:05:33,810 --> 00:05:36,260
nearby town are harder to dismiss together.

165
00:05:36,570 --> 00:05:38,580
You stop asking whether you can prove
everything.

166
00:05:38,930 --> 00:05:41,530
You ask what happens if you wait for perfect
proof.

167
00:05:41,530 --> 00:05:42,570
Then you go shopping.

168
00:05:42,570 --> 00:05:43,300
Water first.

169
00:05:43,850 --> 00:05:45,780
Your cupboards contain things you can eat.

170
00:05:45,810 --> 00:05:48,770
Your taps contain a service somebody else has
to keep running.

171
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:51,300
You buy sealed containers in several sizes.

172
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:52,580
Ones you can lift,

173
00:05:52,930 --> 00:05:54,420
ones you can pour safely.

174
00:05:54,490 --> 00:05:55,610
You keep the receipt.

175
00:05:55,610 --> 00:05:57,660
You still want an ordinary explanation.

176
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:58,180
At home,

177
00:05:58,450 --> 00:06:00,420
the first load barely slows you down.

178
00:06:00,730 --> 00:06:04,170
By the fourth trip your arms are shaking you
stand beside

179
00:06:04,170 --> 00:06:04,650
the car,

180
00:06:04,850 --> 00:06:08,450
looking at the remaining containers, then at
the distance between the driveway

181
00:06:08,450 --> 00:06:09,250
and your kitchen.

182
00:06:09,250 --> 00:06:11,020
20 yards. That is all.

183
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:14,540
You imagine carrying the same load while
somebody chases you.

184
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:16,740
The next container is going to a different
room.

185
00:06:17,130 --> 00:06:20,610
You split the supplies so one blocked doorway
cannot separate

186
00:06:20,610 --> 00:06:21,220
you from everything.

187
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:22,180
Then food,

188
00:06:22,450 --> 00:06:23,500
canned meals,

189
00:06:23,770 --> 00:06:24,380
beans,

190
00:06:24,730 --> 00:06:25,220
fish,

191
00:06:25,730 --> 00:06:29,130
peanut butter. Things requiring little
preparation, a manual

192
00:06:29,130 --> 00:06:31,340
can opener you almost choose the electric one.

193
00:06:31,450 --> 00:06:32,220
You put it back.

194
00:06:32,610 --> 00:06:36,170
By afternoon, a battery radio sits on your
kitchen table beside

195
00:06:36,170 --> 00:06:39,220
a first aid kit and unfamiliar packets of
filters.

196
00:06:39,530 --> 00:06:41,580
Your bank sends a spending notification.

197
00:06:41,690 --> 00:06:42,580
You dismiss it.

198
00:06:42,890 --> 00:06:43,380
For once,

199
00:06:43,730 --> 00:06:44,900
the number isn't the problem.

200
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:46,420
You check the chat.

201
00:06:46,690 --> 00:06:48,140
Most people are still joking.

202
00:06:48,170 --> 00:06:50,100
But two ask where you bought the equipment.

203
00:06:50,250 --> 00:06:51,620
One asks privately.

204
00:06:51,690 --> 00:06:52,540
You answer both.

205
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:54,980
Then you notice Daniel hasn't read anything.

206
00:06:55,210 --> 00:06:56,260
You walk through the house.

207
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:58,540
The front door has a solid lock.

208
00:06:58,890 --> 00:07:00,940
The side gate doesn't close properly.

209
00:07:01,290 --> 00:07:04,610
The rear exit opens onto a narrow garden path
cluttered

210
00:07:04,610 --> 00:07:05,420
with pots.

211
00:07:05,730 --> 00:07:09,300
You spend an hour fixing something you have
ignored for eight months.

212
00:07:09,450 --> 00:07:10,660
Then you clear the path.

213
00:07:10,850 --> 00:07:12,820
A house that keeps people out is useful.

214
00:07:12,930 --> 00:07:15,100
A house you cannot leave is a different
problem.

215
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:17,340
Curtains cover the windows after dark.

216
00:07:17,690 --> 00:07:20,460
Shoes and a packed bag wait near the rear
door.

217
00:07:20,650 --> 00:07:23,700
you move the kitchen extinguisher out from
behind shopping bags.

218
00:07:23,730 --> 00:07:24,940
You test the flashlight.

219
00:07:25,210 --> 00:07:28,850
It works. That tiny circle of light makes you
feel better than the expensive

220
00:07:28,850 --> 00:07:29,660
car outside.

221
00:07:30,490 --> 00:07:32,660
At 9:10, Daniel returns.

222
00:07:32,930 --> 00:07:34,180
Only three messages.

223
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:34,860
Still here?

224
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:37,050
Don't enter places with visible growth.

225
00:07:37,050 --> 00:07:39,410
Don't assume clear looking air proves safety.

226
00:07:39,410 --> 00:07:41,980
If you have somewhere safe to stay, get it
ready now.

227
00:07:42,090 --> 00:07:43,300
You ask whether he can leave.

228
00:07:43,650 --> 00:07:44,380
He doesn't answer.

229
00:07:44,650 --> 00:07:46,500
Someone asks when the prank ends.

230
00:07:46,530 --> 00:07:47,980
Daniel doesn't answer that either

231
00:07:48,450 --> 00:07:49,850
His status disappears.

232
00:07:49,850 --> 00:07:51,460
You wait another 15 minutes.

233
00:07:51,690 --> 00:07:52,660
Then you call your parents.

234
00:07:52,970 --> 00:07:54,650
Your mother answers over the television.

235
00:07:54,650 --> 00:07:57,300
Everything alright? You look at the equipment
covering your table.

236
00:07:57,370 --> 00:07:57,850
Yes.

237
00:07:58,050 --> 00:07:59,690
The word comes out automatically.

238
00:07:59,690 --> 00:08:00,780
You close your eyes.

239
00:08:00,890 --> 00:08:01,370
Actually,

240
00:08:01,650 --> 00:08:02,850
can I come over tomorrow?

241
00:08:02,850 --> 00:08:03,780
Two days remain.

242
00:08:04,130 --> 00:08:07,220
You pack three respirators and compatible
spare filters.

243
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:08,420
One for each parent.

244
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:09,780
One for your little sister.

245
00:08:09,890 --> 00:08:12,020
You think about posting the warning publicly.

246
00:08:12,130 --> 00:08:14,130
Then you open another unavailable video.

247
00:08:14,130 --> 00:08:15,820
You don't know who removed it or why?

248
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:18,980
Your mind supplies the worst explanation.

249
00:08:19,210 --> 00:08:22,530
You imagine being contacted by somebody who
wants to know where Daniel

250
00:08:22,530 --> 00:08:23,010
is,

251
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:26,450
or having your parents address attached to a
post that spreads

252
00:08:26,450 --> 00:08:27,810
farther than you intended.

253
00:08:27,810 --> 00:08:28,900
You close the page.

254
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:30,260
You will tell them in person.

255
00:08:30,530 --> 00:08:33,210
Your father opens the door holding the
television remote.

256
00:08:33,210 --> 00:08:34,020
Are you moving in?

257
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:35,820
You put the bag on the kitchen table.

258
00:08:36,010 --> 00:08:37,610
Your mother sees the masks.

259
00:08:37,610 --> 00:08:40,740
What happened? Your prepared explanation
disappears.

260
00:08:40,810 --> 00:08:44,330
A person I know works at that research
facility outside the city.

261
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:46,220
Your father looks at your orange shirt.

262
00:08:46,450 --> 00:08:47,260
Then the bag.

263
00:08:47,530 --> 00:08:49,860
Please tell me this isn't from your gaming
friends.

264
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:51,620
You show him the public video.

265
00:08:51,890 --> 00:08:53,620
He watches until the first attack.

266
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:55,180
Hands back the phone.

267
00:08:55,250 --> 00:08:57,580
You can make anything look real now, I know.

268
00:08:57,930 --> 00:08:59,300
So why bring this here?

269
00:08:59,410 --> 00:09:00,540
You look toward the hall.

270
00:09:00,730 --> 00:09:02,620
Your sister stands behind the corner.

271
00:09:02,890 --> 00:09:03,820
Not smiling.

272
00:09:04,130 --> 00:09:06,100
Listening. You turn the phone face down.

273
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:08,980
Because having water and food is useful, even
if I'm wrong.

274
00:09:09,250 --> 00:09:11,610
Your mother keeps folding the empty shopping
bag.

275
00:09:11,610 --> 00:09:12,260
How much water?

276
00:09:12,410 --> 00:09:14,780
You explain the emergency guideline you
checked.

277
00:09:14,810 --> 00:09:18,620
About a gallon per person daily for drinking
and other basic uses,

278
00:09:18,650 --> 00:09:20,380
with individual needs varying.

279
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:22,180
Your father starts calculating.

280
00:09:22,330 --> 00:09:22,900
Three people.

281
00:09:23,290 --> 00:09:26,700
Several days. Now the warning takes up space
in his garage.

282
00:09:26,810 --> 00:09:29,340
I didn't say empty the supermarket, you tell
him.

283
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:31,940
Just have enough that you don't need to go out
immediately.

284
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:33,650
Your sister enters the kitchen.

285
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:34,890
Will the masks fit me?

286
00:09:34,890 --> 00:09:36,420
Nobody answers quickly enough.

287
00:09:36,770 --> 00:09:39,060
You sit beside her and check the size you
brought.

288
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:40,140
It isn't right.

289
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:42,380
The lower edge lifts away from her face.

290
00:09:42,650 --> 00:09:43,780
You stare at the gap.

291
00:09:44,050 --> 00:09:45,300
You remember to buy three.

292
00:09:45,490 --> 00:09:47,850
You forgot she wasn't simply a smaller adult.

293
00:09:47,850 --> 00:09:49,380
I'll get the right size, you say.

294
00:09:49,490 --> 00:09:51,140
Your father puts down the remote.

295
00:09:51,290 --> 00:09:53,330
This time, he asks where you bought them.

296
00:09:53,330 --> 00:09:56,340
You stay while the first containers are filled
with safe tap water

297
00:09:56,650 --> 00:10:00,010
your mother makes a shopping list Your father
checks the pantry and

298
00:10:00,010 --> 00:10:03,610
discovers that several cans he counted are
empty tins he kept

299
00:10:03,610 --> 00:10:06,300
for screws. For a minute, everyone laughs.

300
00:10:06,370 --> 00:10:09,860
It feels so normal you almost let the warning
become ridiculous again.

301
00:10:09,970 --> 00:10:12,700
Then your sister asks whether she should pack
her school bag.

302
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:14,530
Your mother stops writing.

303
00:10:14,530 --> 00:10:15,260
Not tonight.

304
00:10:15,530 --> 00:10:16,650
She says it gently.

305
00:10:16,650 --> 00:10:18,700
She doesn't say there is nothing to worry
about.

306
00:10:18,930 --> 00:10:20,860
At the door, she touches your arm.

307
00:10:21,010 --> 00:10:23,860
You're being careful too you nod she looks
toward the car

308
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:26,180
Then stop checking that phone while you drive.

309
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:27,340
You promise.

310
00:10:27,650 --> 00:10:29,140
Your sister follows you outside.

311
00:10:29,290 --> 00:10:30,180
Are you scared?

312
00:10:30,370 --> 00:10:31,100
You look back.

313
00:10:31,450 --> 00:10:33,300
Your father is measuring shelf space.

314
00:10:33,410 --> 00:10:35,060
Your mother is checking the list.

315
00:10:35,210 --> 00:10:36,890
A little. Then why were you joking?

316
00:10:36,890 --> 00:10:38,020
You have no useful answer.

317
00:10:38,370 --> 00:10:40,820
She waits. I thought everybody else knew
something.

318
00:10:40,850 --> 00:10:42,540
I didn't. She considers that.

319
00:10:42,610 --> 00:10:45,140
Then takes your hand and leads you back toward
the door.

320
00:10:45,210 --> 00:10:46,100
Tell Dad again.

321
00:10:46,170 --> 00:10:46,820
So you do.

322
00:10:46,930 --> 00:10:49,340
This time you show him Daniel's video too.

323
00:10:49,530 --> 00:10:50,740
He watches the whole thing.

324
00:10:50,850 --> 00:10:53,380
Then he asks you to send the address of the
supplier.

325
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:53,930
At home,

326
00:10:54,210 --> 00:10:56,620
you arrange a fitting for your sister the
following morning.

327
00:10:56,930 --> 00:10:59,220
You put the car keys beside your packed bag.

328
00:10:59,250 --> 00:11:00,420
Then you open the chat.

329
00:11:00,490 --> 00:11:01,140
9:08.

330
00:11:01,570 --> 00:11:02,540
Daniel isn't there.

331
00:11:03,210 --> 00:11:05,700
9:10. Someone writes, You alive?

332
00:11:06,530 --> 00:11:08,900
9:13. Another mushroom sticker.

333
00:11:09,010 --> 00:11:12,500
Nobody reacts. At 9:17, a message appears.

334
00:11:12,570 --> 00:11:13,580
From Daniel's account.

335
00:11:13,810 --> 00:11:14,700
This is Mara.

336
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:16,500
Daniel is helping hold the door.

337
00:11:16,650 --> 00:11:17,580
You sit forward.

338
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:19,700
He told me to send this if we had to move.

339
00:11:20,130 --> 00:11:21,460
A photograph follows.

340
00:11:21,650 --> 00:11:24,380
A paper map marked reported exposures.

341
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:27,340
One circle surrounds the town from the public
video.

342
00:11:27,650 --> 00:11:29,460
Another marks the junction near your parents.

343
00:11:29,890 --> 00:11:31,740
Beside it, Daniel has written

344
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:34,970
reported yesterday. Facility transport
vehicle.

345
00:11:34,970 --> 00:11:36,340
Mara sends one more line.

346
00:11:36,530 --> 00:11:39,530
The first exposed people left before the
building was sealed.

347
00:11:39,530 --> 00:11:41,420
You look at the water beside your pantry.

348
00:11:41,570 --> 00:11:44,100
The bag waiting by the door, your keys,

349
00:11:44,490 --> 00:11:46,580
then your phone lights up with an incoming
call.

350
00:11:47,050 --> 00:11:49,300
Dad, you answer before the second ring.

351
00:11:49,370 --> 00:11:50,860
The mask, he says.

352
00:11:51,170 --> 00:11:52,300
He isn't laughing now.

353
00:11:52,410 --> 00:11:54,380
Can you get the right one for your sister
tonight?

354
00:11:54,410 --> 00:11:57,740
Behind him, you hear your mother asking him to
step away from the window.

355
00:11:57,970 --> 00:11:58,500
You stand.

356
00:11:58,930 --> 00:11:59,740
What happened?

357
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:01,460
The neighbor across the road.

358
00:12:01,810 --> 00:12:02,580
A pause.

359
00:12:03,090 --> 00:12:05,620
He's been standing beside his car for 20
minutes.

360
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:06,900
You pick up the keys.

361
00:12:07,010 --> 00:12:08,380
Your father lowers his voice.

362
00:12:08,850 --> 00:12:10,460
And somebody just tried to help him.
